Since no one else has said this yet I will say it (spoiler follows):

the trick is to become chaotic if you aren't already.  When going up with the
amulet in Gehennom, wear that helm of opposite alignment you have saved up and
ditch it when you leave Gehennom.  Chaotics have little trouble going up with
the amulet in Gehennom, neutrals some trouble and lawfuls a lot of trouble.

As I read the code, everytime one goes up with the amulet in Gehennom there is
a 1 in 4 chance of something unusual happening instead of actually going up.
Chaotics are teleported randomly within the same level (having teleport control
has no affect here).  Lawfuls are dropped from 1 to 3 levels (chosen randomly).
For neutrals the chances are split 50/50 between teleported within that level
or being dropped from 1 to 3 levels.  Thus a lawful will make slow progress.

In olden days (pre 3.1) when Gehennom was called hell and was the realm of the
chaotic god rather than the present unaligned god chaotics were not afflicted
at all when they went up with the amulet.  Even now chaotics are favored,
although not as much.

